    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1401">

                <pb facs="0928" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg812"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/271.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Ambassador to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spanish Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Minister of Spain to Mexico
                    wires me that the Spanish colony of the port of Guaymas consisting of about two
                    hundred persons is completely shut out from communication with our
                    representative at the capital of the neighboring Republic and fears that it may
                    be left without adequate protection if the town should be taken by the
                    revolutionists.</p>
                <p>In view thereof I have recourse to your excellency’s courtesy and beg you kindly
                    to instruct the Consul of the United States at Guaymas, Sonora, Mexico, to
                    protect the said Spanish subjects when necessary.</p>
                <p>Thanking your excellency in advance, I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan Riaño</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
